FILED s522b (Opus, 2026-10-19) from Fable's s522 merge probe b4-method-replace.pl r5.  PRE-EXISTING; NOT the method-install path (member 3 of s522b), so filed, not folded.

    package P3; sub m { "old" } package main; undef &P3::m;
    print "r5 ", (P3->can("m") ? "can" : "cannot"), " ", (eval { P3->m; "ran" } // "died"), "\n";

perl 5.40.3: `r5 can died`.  PCL: `r5 cannot died`.  p-undef-sub fmakunbound's the symbol and records :was-defined in *p-declared-subs* (so `exists &P3::m` stays true); `can` asks fboundp and misses.  Fix direction: `can` returns a code ref for a :was-defined sub that dies "Undefined subroutine &P3::m called" when called -- check what perl's message is for calling the can() result first.
